[SAFETY_GOAL]
UID: SG-09
STATEMENT: >>>
Detection shall remain effective when any single detection channel is absent or has failed.
<<<
LAYERS: L2 thermal + L2 current
COMMENT: >>>
The one goal realised by no single requirement. It is a property of the
arrangement rather than of any clause: the thermal and the electrical channel
use different sensors and different physical principles, and
[`safety.md` §6](safety.md#6-independence) makes it a standing constraint that
neither may be removed on the grounds that the other exists. The nearest thing
to a requirement behind it is that constraint.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HZ-01
  ROLE: Mitigates
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HZ-03
  ROLE: Mitigates
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: HZ-09
  ROLE: Mitigates

[SAFETY_GOAL]
UID: SG-10
STATEMENT: >>>
Every threshold shall be bounded, no detection shall be disableable, and rules shall be specified so that a healthy firing does not trip them.
<<<
LAYERS: L2 rule design
COMMENT: >>>
Also realised by the confirmation windows of
[`safety.md` §7.3](safety.md#73-why-two-rules-carry-a-confirmation-window), which
are rule design rather than a separate clause.
<<<
